#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:46 f9c1075599aa4d40b545c1c971e0a9f5
msgid "**SLOT**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:46 abcebe4a32e6421d85995577cf283519
msgid "Where the cartridge sits. A tape in a drive shows the drive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:47 b2566ae774e34677adcc0bb584ae0b7d
msgid "**KIND**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:47 55749cb4ecc5400baaf8a7e9a4205ae5
msgid "``data``, ``clean`` or ``WORM``, from the barcode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:48 d90c1e79c95046b7b866c71c665420bb
msgid "**DENSITY**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:48 efe1d1e8ccc84103986d98a70e2c7566
msgid "The generation, from the barcode suffix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:49 37cc8c7ffd5d43788b4695d062902566
msgid "**USED MB**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:49 3272ab2cffdd49b3b369177e901d87eb
msgid "How much of it has been written - the size of its files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:50 0db5de6f63cd44c695e82982d377c324
msgid "**CAPACITY MB**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:50 429e9d9e230340e78246950d71654b32
msgid "How big it was made"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:51 5a05ce503f014b37a29a2c4f97b306b8
msgid "**ON DISK**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:51 517a7cbd3f444438acc8666a80813d59
msgid ""
"Whether its files are really there. ``no`` means the library lists a tape"
" whose files are gone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:56 e68cea91d7c3478c9e3d43b7c359b217
msgid "Where the numbers come from"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:58 5bcc025da26f4ee9b33550eefb80c849
msgid ""
"**Used** is the size of the tape's data files under "
"``/opt/mhvtl/<barcode>/``. It is what is really on the disk, which is "
"what matters when the disk fills up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:62 1440a35c76924f83830a611d67b09d93
msgid ""
"**Capacity** is read from the cartridge's own MAM file - the medium "
"auxiliary memory, which a real cartridge also has. That is why a tape "
"sitting in a slot has a size at all: nothing needs to load it to ask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:66 5bd802fa6ff146e58cbb126bfeb47a2e
msgid ""
"A tape in a drive has a second, better answer: the drive itself, which is"
" live while a backup runs. The two disagree during a write - the MAM is "
"only written back when the tape is unloaded - and the drive is right. See"
" :doc:`../using/watching`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:72 e4ec763cf260413da7c19301f1066c9d
msgid "Compression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/inventory.rst:74 e9ad2dd502bc4bc8b1df2f3e0d24e1f3
msgid ""
"MHVTL compresses what it writes, so a tape holds more than its size in "
"data: 600 MB of ordinary files takes about 285 MB of a cartridge. The "
"drive reports the ratio while it writes, and the tape's *used* figure is "
"the compressed size, because that is what occupies the disk."
msgstr ""

